    "_manual_notes": "The AAQH-Saving subscale comprises odd-numbered items (1,3,5,7,9,11,13) and the AAQH-Acquisition subscale comprises even-numbered items (2,4,6,8,10,12,14). All items are forward-scored. The total score is the sum of both subscales."
  },
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "lk_1": "Never true",
      "lk_2": "Very seldom true",
      "lk_3": "Seldom true",
      "lk_4": "Sometimes true",
      "lk_5": "Frequently true",
      "lk_6": "Almost always true",
      "lk_7": "Always true",
      "question_head": "Below you will find a list of statements that have to do with how you feel about the things you own. Please rate how true each statement is for you within the past week.",
      "aaqh_1": "I need to stop feeling so attached to my things.",
      "aaqh_2": "I get lost in my thoughts about buying or finding something I really want.",
      "aaqh_3": "I can't stand feeling like I might make a mistake if I get rid of something.",
      "aaqh_4": "My thoughts or feelings about my things control my actions.",
      "aaqh_5": "I have a hard time getting rid of things even when I know I should.",
      "aaqh_6": "My things are a central part of who I am.",
      "aaqh_7": "My thoughts or feelings make it hard for me to get rid of my things.",
      "aaqh_8": "I need to get rid of my urges to acquire new things.",
      "aaqh_9": "I struggle to get rid of items that feel important to me.",
      "aaqh_10": "I am always thinking about my things.",
      "aaqh_11": "If I am worried I might need something in the future, I keep it.",
      "aaqh_12": "I continue to collect items, even when they cause problems for me.",
      "aaqh_13": "I keep my things because I am attached to them.",
      "aaqh_14": "I collect or buy objects when I feel distressed."
    }
  }
}